{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 7, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the chirping of birds, a sound strangely…crisp. Sunlight streamed through a window, illuminating dust motes dancing in the air. He sat up, a familiar ache in his lower back, but something was off. The colors seemed too vibrant, the details too sharp. He looked around his bedroom, noticing the perfectly symmetrical arrangement of his books, the unnaturally clean lines of his furniture. A notification box popped into his vision, hovering above his desk: \"Quest Available: Retrieve Lost Kitten.\" He blinked, and the box vanished. He tried to reach for his glasses, but his hand passed right through the desk. Panic began to bubble in his chest as he realized the impossible: he wasn't in his bedroom anymore. He was *in* it. He was inside a video game.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of his room, finding the world outside equally unreal. The trees in his garden were rendered with meticulous detail, every leaf individually defined. People walked by with a slightly jerky gait, their conversations punctuated by repetitive phrases. A quest marker appeared above a woman watering her petunias: \"NPC - Gardener - Potential Quest Giver.\" Arthur felt a wave of disorientation wash over him. He tried to speak, but his voice came out sounding strangely synthesized, a digital echo of his own. This wasn't a dream; it was a meticulously crafted world, and he was trapped inside it, forced to play a role he hadn't chosen. He had no idea how to escape, or even what the objective was, but one thing was clear: his life had irrevocably changed.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -1.5287038087844849}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.062007613480091095}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.003255189396440983}, {"token": "▁chir", "logprob": -0.16917015612125397}, {"token": "ping", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "